					<div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content"><div class="mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang="en" dir="ltr" data-mw-parsoid-version="0.24.0.0-alpha27" data-mw-html-version="2.8.0"><section data-mw-section-id="0" id="mwAQ"><div class="shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux" style="display:none" about="#mwt1" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Short description","href":"./Template:Short_description"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Telecommunications company"}},"i":0}}]}'>Telecommunications company</div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_short_description"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Short_description_is_different_from_Wikidata"/></span>
<span about="#mwt2" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lowercase title","href":"./Template:Lowercase_title"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></span>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Infobox company\n","href":"./Template:Infobox_company"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"iQ Group"},"logo":{"wt":"IQ group Logo.jpg"},"type":{"wt":"Telecommunications"},"founded":{"wt":"2005"},"area_served":{"wt":"Middle East"},"key_people":{"wt":"[[Asoz Latif Rashid]] (CEO)"},"website":{"wt":"{{URL|https://iq.group/}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1358620234" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt4" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Infobox/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>@media(min-width:640px){.mw-parser-output .infobox{margin-left:1em;float:right;clear:right;width:22em}}.mw-parser-output .infobox-subbox{padding:0;border:none;margin:-3px;width:auto;min-width:100%;font-size:100%;clear:none;float:none;background-color:transparent;color:inherit}.mw-parser-output .infobox-3cols-child{margin:-3px}.mw-parser-output .infobox .navbar{font-size:100%}.mw-parser-output .infobox-hiddenrow,body.skin--responsive.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox .infobox-hiddenrow{display:none}@media screen{html.skin-theme-clientpref-night .mw-parser-output .infobox-full-data:not(.notheme)>div:not(.notheme)[style]{background:#1f1f23!important;color:#f8f9fa}}@media screen and (prefers-color-scheme:dark){html.skin-theme-clientpref-os .mw-parser-output .infobox-full-data:not(.notheme)>div:not(.notheme)[style]{background:#1f1f23!important;color:#f8f9fa}}@media(min-width:640px){body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table{display:table!important}body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table>caption{display:table-caption!important}body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table>tbody{display:table-row-group}body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table th,body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table td{padding-left:inherit;padding-right:inherit}}</style><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1326365004" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt5" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Infobox company/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .ib-company .infobox-label{padding-right:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .ib-company-logo img{background-color:#f8f9fa;color:inherit}.mw-parser-output .ib-company-logo .logo-nobg img{background-color:inherit;color:inherit}.mw-parser-output .ib-company-locality,.mw-parser-output .ib-company-country{display:inline}</style></span><table class="infobox ib-company vcard" about="#mwt3" id="mwBQ"><tbody><tr><th colspan="2" class="infobox-above fn org">iQ Group</th></tr><tr><td colspan="2" class="infobox-image ib-company-logo logo"><span class="mw-default-size logo-nobg" typeof="mw:File/Frameless"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:IQ_group_Logo.jpg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:IQ_group_Logo.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/IQ_group_Logo.jpg/250px-IQ_group_Logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/IQ_group_Logo.jpg/500px-IQ_group_Logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2084" data-file-height="2084" data-file-type="bitmap" height="250" width="250" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 1"/></a></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label">Type</th><td class="infobox-data category">Telecommunications</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label">Founded</th><td class="infobox-data">2005</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label"><div style="display: inline-block; line-height: 1.2em; padding: .1em 0; ">Area served</div></th><td class="infobox-data">Middle East</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label">Key<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>people</th><td class="infobox-data agent"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asoz_Latif_Rashid" title="Asoz Latif Rashid">Asoz Latif Rashid</a> (CEO)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label">Website</th><td class="infobox-data"><span class="url"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://iq.group/" class="external text">iq<wbr/>.group</a></span></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p id="mwBg"><b id="mwBw">iQ Group</b> (also known as <b id="mwCA">iQ</b>) is an Iraqi technology conglomerate founded in 2005.<sup about="#mwt8" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-1" id="mwCQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDA">]</span></span></a></sup> The company was initially established as a fibre-optic <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_service_provider" title="Internet service provider" id="mwDQ">internet service provider</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sulaymaniyah" title="Sulaymaniyah" id="mwDg">Sulaymaniyah</a>, Iraq.<sup about="#mwt11" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-2" id="mwDw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQ">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwEw" aria-labelledby="History"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="History">History</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=IQ_Group&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: History"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwFA">Founded in 2005, iQ began by building <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibre_Optic" title="Fibre Optic" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFQ">fibre-optic</a> topology and cable routes across the country<sup about="#mwt14" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-3" id="mwFg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGA">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGQ">]</span></span></a></sup> to be able to provide internet services in Iraq. IQ Group provides fibre-optic broadband services and wholesales capacity services to a range of customers, including businesses, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-governmental_organization" title="Non-governmental organization" id="mwGg">NGOs</a>, schools, hospitals.<sup about="#mwt17" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-4" id="mwGw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHQ">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHg">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2020, with the arrival of the new CEO, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asoz_Latif_Rashid" title="Asoz Latif Rashid" id="mwHw">Asoz Latif Rashid</a>, iQ group began to work in new areas.<sup about="#mwt20" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-5" id="mwIA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIg">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIw">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2023, it launched a partnership with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tencent" title="Tencent" id="mwJA">Tencent</a>.<sup about="#mwt23" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-6" id="mwJQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJw">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwKQ" aria-labelledby="Transit_connectivity"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Transit_connectivity">Transit connectivity</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=IQ_Group&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Transit connectivity"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwKg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:IQ_Group_Silk_Route_transit_map.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwKw"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:IQ_Group_Silk_Route_transit_map.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/IQ_Group_Silk_Route_transit_map.png/250px-IQ_Group_Silk_Route_transit_map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/IQ_Group_Silk_Route_transit_map.png/500px-IQ_Group_Silk_Route_transit_map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2667" data-file-height="1500" data-file-type="bitmap" height="141" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLA"/></a><figcaption id="mwLQ">IQ Group Silk Route transit map</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwLg">IQ Group's Silk Route Transit is a terrestrial fibre-optic infrastructure IP-Transit project that provides an alternative route to connect Europe and the Middle East.<sup about="#mwt26" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-7"}}'><a href="#cite_note-7" id="mwLw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMQ">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwMw">Conceptualised in 2010, the Silk Route Transit consists of over 3500 kilometers of fiber-optic cable<sup about="#mwt29" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-8" id="mwNA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNg">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNw">]</span></span></a></sup> laid across Iraq.<sup about="#mwt32" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-9"}}'><a href="#cite_note-9" id="mwOA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwOQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOg">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOw">]</span></span></a></sup> Its multilayer fiber-optic network supposedly provides the shortest alternative terrestrial route to connect Europe to Asia.<sup about="#mwt35" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-10" id="mwPA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPg">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt38" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-11"}}'><a href="#cite_note-11" id="mwQA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQg">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwRA" aria-labelledby="References"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="References">References</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=IQ_Group&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: References"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

